content": "", "type": "text"}], "correct_feedback": "Correct!"}, "type": "feedback"}, {"type": "learning_skills", "contents": [{"content": "Reading", "type": "skill"}, {"content": "Writing", "type": "skill"}, {"content": "Speaking", "type": "skill"}]}, {"type": "post_instructions", "contents": [{"content": "Instructions: Complete the following steps. Fill in the Self-Assessment.", "type": "text"}]}]}], "_data": [{"type": "lab_options", "contents": [{"content": true, "type": "has_nav"}, {"content": true, "type": "has_exercise_controls"}]}]}], "type": "sena", "_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"content": "", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "While Loops in JavaScript", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 8, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 3, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "B1.2", "type": "level"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": "These are words you use to talk about JavaScript loops.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"content": "Understand information about web applications, their principles and basic concepts in a range of work contexts.   Describe applications for an operating system for personal computers in a range of work contexts.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": "Discusses a range of options for potential actions at work through the correct use of grammar, vocabulary; level of formality and purpose, and cohesion and coherence aspects appropriate to this level.  Exchanges simple information on web applications, and applications for operating systems for personal computers.", "type": "secondary_1"}]}, {"content": "enpe7n6le03ob08re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Negative Imperatives", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "<strong>Imperatives</strong> are used to give orders, make suggestions or invite someone to do something.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "We may have heard or used <b>imperatives</b> many times without realizing what they are. We can use them for different purposes and its grammatical structure is very simple.<br/><br/>They use the base form of the verb at the beginning of the sentence without a subject. They are not conjugated in any tense. If you need to make a <b>negative imperative</b>, you only need to add the auxiliary verb \u201c<strong>do</strong>\u201d with the particle \u201c<strong>not</strong>\u201d contracted or not at the beginning of the sentence. Let's check the structure:<br/><br/><div class=\"center_text\"><span class=\"strong\">Do + not + base form of verb + complement</span></div> ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Do not forget to use the \"while\" keyword. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Do not confuse these loops. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Do not omit the breaks.", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Adjectives Ending in \u2013Ed and \u2013Ing", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "Verbs can become <strong>adjectives</strong> by adding <strong>\u2013ed</strong> or <strong>-ing</strong>", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "It is possible to turn a verb into an <b>adjective</b> with the use of those suffixes. Because they are <b>adjectives</b>, they are used along with the verb to be but be careful because meaning changes. Let's take a look at some examples:<br/><br/><div class=\"center_text\"><span class=\"italic\">I'm sure people might be <strong>interested</strong> in more advice.</span></div><br/><br/>In the example, people feel \u201cinterested\u201d in a certain way.<br/><br/><div class=\"center_text\"><span class=\"italic\">It's more <strong>boring</strong> to check twice before launching.</span></div><br/><br/>In this example, something has the characteristic of \u201cboring\u201d.<br/><br/>When you use a <strong>\u2013ing adjective</strong>, it means that the subject has the characteristic. When you use the <strong>\u2013ed adjective</strong>, it means that the subject feels in a certain manner.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Since programming can be too demanding sometimes.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "I quitted because at a point it got really tiring to work over something endlessly.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "You may feel more satisfied by being extra careful when writing in JavaScript.", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "demanding ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "that requires a lot of effort  ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example:  Since programming can be too demanding sometimes, you may need to use strategic statements to reduce the work.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n6le03ob08aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "endlessly ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "that happens in a continuous way without stopping  ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adverb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I've done programming but I quitted because at a point it got really tiring to work over something endlessly.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n6le03ob08aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "ease down ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to make something easier or reduce the complexity and therefore, the effort needed  ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(phrasal verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: For such task, loops really ease down the burden of writing the same multiple times.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n6le03ob08aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "alike", "type": "name"}, {"content": "very similar in characteristics ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: There are multiple types of loops in JavaScript, the first two are the most common and are alike. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n6le03ob08aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "misspelled ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "something written incorrectly  ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: It's more boring to check twice before launching, but it's also more difficult to find a misspelled code once it's been finished.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n6le03ob08aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "mess ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "disorder, dirtiness, disorganization  ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: And please, do not confuse these loops, they are alike, as I said, but in programming they can make a mess if they are not used properly.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n6le03ob08aud06", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "Search for more information about while loops in JavaScript. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Create a poster where you include features from the while loops. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "On a separate poster include features from the do-while loops. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Share your work with the class. ", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"content": "I use while loops in JavaScript.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I identify the syntax of the while loops. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I understand the purposes of the loops. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": " I share my work with the class. ", "type": "text"}]}]}